  "agent": {
    "note": "**Debugger removed; the inspector now shows the hidden engine state.** Per your call: X/Y/W/H/Z fully describe ONE rect, so they're the **output** section on top; everything else is parser bookkeeping, so it sits **below a labelled `ENGINE STATE` divider**. The inspector fills the whole right column now — no separate debugger panel.\n\n**The three internal vars (the stuff nothing showed before):**\n\n| field | what it is | when it moves |\n|---|---|---|\n| **N** | split arity (cols/rows) | on each count read |\n| **R** | **quantization remainder** — leftover px when a split doesn't divide evenly | on uneven splits |\n| **C** | **passthrough carry** — px a `0`/`>` donates forward, claimed by the next tile | donate → claim |\n\n**This layout is seeded to exercise both** (I'll keep pre-seeding stress strings so you don't hand-edit): `2[7(F,0,F,F,F,F,F),9(F,F,F,F,F,>,F,F,F)]` — the **7-split → R=2**, the **9-split → R=3** (1920 ÷ 7 and ÷ 9 don't divide evenly), and each row has a passthrough so **C** visibly fills then empties as a later tile absorbs it.\n\n**One honest finding:** the parse trace doesn't actually expose split metadata (no remainder/requested/resolved on the events), so **R is computed from geometry** (`extent % count`) — exact for uniform splits, which is the tutorial's bread and butter. C is reconstructed from the donation flow.\n\n*(160 tests green incl. new R/C coverage. Verified the two-section layout + divider render; C pulses green on donate/claim.)*",
    "question": "Does the split-pane inspector read well — output rect on top, `ENGINE STATE` divider, then N/R/C — and do R (watch it hit 2 on the 7-split, 3 on the 9-split) and C (fills on the `0`/`>`, empties on the next tile) tell the hidden-state story clearly? If yes, that's the last panel done and we can move to the big perf review. If the divider/labels/values need tuning, say so.",
    "context": {
      "category": {
        "kind": "other",
        "label": "inspector-engine-state"
      },
      "intent": {
        "action": "propose",
        "summary": "Remove the debugger; extend the inspector into Output (X/Y/W/H/Z, one rect) + ENGINE STATE divider + Internal (N arity, R quantization remainder, C passthrough carry). R computed from geometry; C from the donation flow."
      },
      "relation": {
        "kind": "refines",
        "target": "020"
      }
    }
  }
